/-
D30 — the original-polynomial identities, split out of `Compatibility`
======================================================================

Coordinator instruction (parallel/D30/TASK.md, 2026-09-12 02:57): the identities from
`p1_poly_compat` through `original_iff` depend only on the accepted `Circuit` layer and the
original D05 `CandidateBox`, but the parent module's top-level `import ... Instance` made the
whole file wait for the Jet bounds branch.  This submodule carries exactly those declarations,
unchanged in name, namespace and mathematical content, so that the original-equation
compatibility layer can be compiled and self-reviewed in parallel with JetBounds.

Nothing here assumes a critical point: no `Instance`, no `criticalPoint`, no existence result.
`Compatibility.lean` keeps the tail that genuinely needs `Instance`.
-/
